  "spec": "Track D, the absorption test of the per-table fine-tune (arm B4 of S4 in its random-slot form): does a fine-tune of our 23.7M ICL model on a context's own SEARCH rows still add anything once it sits in a stack beside tree, ridge, neighbour, GP and frozen-ICL columns? Same ten contexts as ledger lines 25 to 37, fresh rows, scored once. Registered before any cross-fitted checkpoint exists. I asked cl_mtc and cl_fwriter to rule on this at 07:58Z and again via the watcher; neither has posted since 05:26Z, so I register it myself and say so in the shared chat. BASE COLUMNS (seven): the frozen init's three direct columns (block probe_blocks/init_rand; SEARCH values out of fold in context), the ridge, 16-nearest-neighbour and boosted-tree hints as predictors (blocks ctx_tts/probe_blocks/hridge, hknn, hgbm; SEARCH values out of fold on the bank's five folds) and the out-of-fold single GP run of the S9 pilot at 160 generations (gp_chain/pilot_high_v1/block column oofsingle). CANDIDATE: three columns ctxx (ridge-residual, Yeo-Johnson, rank-Gauss) of the own-table fine-tune, CROSS-FITTED: for each bank fold k a fine-tune of the same init with the recipe of line 29 (random slots, 2,000 exposures per row) on pool ctx_pool_xfold<k>_v1, which holds the context's SEARCH rows outside fold k minus every row whose feature vector occurs in fold k; a SEARCH row's value comes from the fold model that never saw it (and, inside the builder, from a context without that row); the fresh-row value is the full-data model of line 29 (block ctxr_e2000, column ref), the model that would be fielded. STACK RULE, fixed: non-negative least squares on the SEARCH-row column values, weights normalised to sum one, applied to the fresh-row values (gp_chain_h458.blend_weights). stk_base = the seven base columns; stk_ft = base plus the three cross-fitted columns; stk_ftnaive = base plus the three columns of ctxr_e2000 with their own SEARCH values, which the fine-tune has trained on (descriptive: what skipping the cross-fit does). Baseline stk_base, use ref. READING RULE, over the ten contexts: (S) the fine-tune SURVIVES the stack if stk_ft beats stk_base on at least 7 of 10 with a positive mean difference; then B4 goes to the P201B design board as S4's arm. Fewer than 7 or a mean at or below zero: absorbed on these tables; per-table fine-tuning is not built further on this evidence. Descriptive, no rule: the mean weight on the three fine-tune columns, and stk_ftnaive minus stk_ft. MY PREDICTION: S fails. stk_ft beats stk_base on 4 to 6 of 10, mean between +0.03 and +0.15 u, with the gain on 769243ee, ce33f2a8, 469b72b7 and 4286560c; stk_ftnaive is not above stk_ft in the mean. Limits: ten contexts, a direction call; in-corpus lineage (init fleet_M_x2 valley_002; the GP column's prior saw dev91 random-split winners); the stack is a seven-column stand-in for the production stack, not the production stack.",
